00:23:38,480 --> 00:23:43,480
environmental balance or the ecological balance as it is also known.

237
00:23:44,420 --> 00:23:51,100
Many of these waste products can be prevented or disposed of sensibly, but clearly,

238
00:23:51,520 --> 00:23:56,920
while more and more new and complex goods are produced, there will be new, dangerous

239
00:23:56,920 --> 00:24:02,440
wastes to be disposed of, for example, the waste products from nuclear power

240
00:24:02,440 --> 00:24:09,560
stations. Many people therefore see pollution as only part of a larger and more

241
00:24:09,560 --> 00:24:15,460
complex problem, that is, the whole process of industrial production and consumption

242
00:24:15,460 --> 00:24:21,810
of goods. Others, again, see the problem mainly in connection with agriculture,

243
00:24:22,300 --> 00:24:28,160
where new methods are helping farmers grow more and more on their land to feed our

244
00:24:28,160 --> 00:24:30,160
ever -increasing populations.

245
00:24:31,140 --> 00:24:37,100
However, the land itself, if gradually becoming worn out as it is being used in some

246
00:24:37,100 --> 00:24:40,540
cases too heavily, cannot restore the balance.

247
00:24:41,300 --> 00:24:46,380
Whatever the underlying reasons are, there is no doubt that much of the pollution

248
00:24:46,380 --> 00:24:52,700
caused could be controlled if only companies, individuals and governments would make

249
00:24:52,700 --> 00:24:59,260
more efforts. In the home, there is an obvious need to control litter and waste.

250
00:25:00,160 --> 00:25:05,920
Food comes wrapped up three or four times in packages that all have to be disposed

251
00:25:05,920 --> 00:25:12,980
of. Drinks are increasingly sold in bottles or tins, which cannot be reused.

252
00:25:14,200 --> 00:25:20,340
This not only causes a litter problem, but also is a great waste of resources in

253
00:25:20,340 --> 00:25:23,680
terms of glass, metals and paper.

254
00:25:24,720 --> 00:25:30,720
Advertising has helped this process by persuading many of us not only to buy things

255
00:25:30,720 --> 00:25:36,620
we neither want nor need, but also to throw away much of what we do buy.

256
00:25:37,840 --> 00:25:44,140
Pollution and waste continue to be a problem everyone can help to solve by cutting

257
00:25:44,140 --> 00:25:51,480
out unnecessary buying, excess consumption and careless disposal of the products we

258
00:25:51,480 --> 00:25:53,020
use in our daily life.

